# What seating the chat pack on the 2004 filter strip changes on purpose.
#
#   gate_diff.py --expect tools/porcelain_gate/expect/desktop-frame-chatstrip.expect <pairs...>
#
# Baseline: the commit this branch left, captured with the same binary family
# and the same harness. Do NOT concatenate this with gameframe-layout.expect:
# that file declares what the PORT changed against the pre-port commit, and
# every one of its lines would be stale against this baseline -- which the
# comparator fails on, correctly.
#
# Every line here is a claim a reader is meant to be able to disagree with.
#
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. The chat pack is seated ON the 2004 filter strip, not above it.
#
# Classic Fixed gave the lane's 519-wide pack the 2004 chat hole's own 96
# rows. The pack's eight filters therefore ended at 453 and the frame's own
# filter strip stood below them -- its parchment lip at 453, its button band
# at 467 -- so the player saw a filter row, a pale ledge, and a second row of
# sockets. The pack now takes the hole AND the strip, 17,357 519x146: 357 + 96
# + 50 = 503 is the canvas's last row, so nothing of the frame's bar band is
# left beside the pack's, and 146 - 23 = 123 rows of backing puts the pack's
# own 23-row bar on row 480 -- which is exactly the row interface 548 puts
# that same bar on when it draws its own frame.
#
# THE CLAIM: every line below is interface 162 or the toplevel slot that
# holds it, and every one of them is the same component with the same size
# relationship to its parent, fifty rows further down or fifty rows taller.
# The eight filters are the lane's, all eight of them, on the hollows the
# dressing already cuts; nothing is hidden here that was not hidden before.
# They are written out rather than normalised away because a rule that dropped
# the box from a BOUNDS line would stop the gate noticing a component that
# really did move.
#
# 2. The composed band over the hollows is retired (`abs=0,467 536x32`, and
#    `owned-drop piece.13` below).
#
# 3. The screenshot plugin's camera button follows the bar it sits above
#    (`abs=483,433` -> `abs=483,483`, and `owned-move camera_report` below).

only-before BOUNDS com=0x0224000b (548|11) type=18 graphic=-1 hidden=0 abs=17,357 519x96 wh=519,165 modes=w0,h0,x0,y0 scroll=0x0 off=0,0 = the chat pack in the 2004 hole alone, with the frame's filter strip standing below its bar
only-before BOUNDS com=0xffffffff (65535|65535) type=15 graphic=-1 hidden=0 abs=0,467 536x32 wh=536,32 modes=w0,h0,x-1,y-1 scroll=-1x-1 off=0,0 = the composed band over the 2004 hollows, retired: it tiled 29 columns that carry the first hollow's shadow, so it WAS the row of sockets it was meant to cover
