# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The same three differences, said about the roles and the owned controls
# rather than about the capture lines.
#
# Fifteen roles move and they are the pack's own: the bar, the backing, the
# input line, the eight filter plates and the Report plate's action role. The
# role names are spelled per lane by the profile, so they are named here one
# by one rather than by a prefix -- a prefix would also excuse a role this
# change has nothing to do with.
role-move frame_chat = the pack seated on the strip; @see the capture lines above
role-move chat_backing = its parchment, 73 rows becoming 123
role-move chat_bar = its filter bar, on row 480, where 548 puts that bar on its own frame
role-move chat_input = the typing line, fifty rows down with the rest of the pack
role-move chat_plate_0 = filter 1, moved with the bar it stands on
role-move chat_plate_1 = filter 2, moved with the bar it stands on
role-move chat_plate_2 = filter 3, moved with the bar it stands on
role-move chat_plate_3 = filter 4, moved with the bar it stands on
role-move chat_plate_4 = filter 5, moved with the bar it stands on
role-move chat_plate_5 = filter 6, moved with the bar it stands on
role-move chat_plate_6 = filter 7, moved with the bar it stands on
role-move chat_plate_7 = filter 8 (Report), moved with the bar it stands on
role-move public_chat_button = the same plate under the name the profile gives its action
role-move report_button = the same plate under the name the profile gives its action
role-move action_frame_chat_button_report_activate = Report's activation role, on the plate that moved

# The band itself. `piece.13` is the layout's thirteenth blit and it was that
# picture; the layout now states twelve, and there is no thirteenth key.
owned-drop piece.13 = the composed band over the 2004 hollows, retired: nothing is left for it to cover once the pack's bar stands on them

# And the one control of another plugin's that follows the bar.
owned-move camera_report = the screenshot button sits one row above the pack's filter bar and went with it, 433 to 483

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The composed art lands in different image slots on the remount lanes.
#
# Every box, every size and every hidden bit is identical; what moved is the
# internal slot number the client hands a picture. The describe now states
# nothing on the fence a new frame root appears, so the pictures that fence
# would have named are requested and released one fence later and everything
# allocated afterwards renumbers.
#
# THE CLAIM, stated so it can be argued with: a slot id is an internal handle
# and not behaviour. Nothing reads it, nothing persists it, and no two builds
# are obliged to agree on it. It is the same line the two ports before this
# one carry, for the same reason.
normalise scene = the image slot is an internal handle, and a describe that states nothing on a remount fence renumbers what is allocated after it
